Doomball is a pinball table in prerendered 2.5D with a status panel beside it, with art and sound of its own in the spirit of early-90s shooters.

Missions promote you from Private to General, demons roam a pit of toxic sludge, and three keys open the gate to a three-ball multiball.

The game core is platform independent: it renders into a framebuffer and reads a small input struct, so a port only implements the platform layer. Releases are for Windows, on x86_64 and arm64.

